# Settings ▸ General ▸ Pages ▸ Margin (Ideas #366, whyady): the room round the pages, 1 to 10 pt. A seeded 4 pt
# puts the card 4 pt in from the window's top, right and bottom beside the sidebar, and on every side with the
# sidebar hidden, still rounded and not filling the window. Moved while Cra runs, the window follows at once,
# and Edge to edge still takes the margin away whatever the slider says. The page window's own corners stay inside
# the window's at a narrow margin (Victor, 23 Nov 2026: at 3 pt they stood out at the top and bottom right).
budget rss=600 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "pageMargin": 4}
cra://open?url=${ORIGIN}/page.html
wait 3
cra://debug?windowState=margin4-sidebar
expect-log window state margin4-sidebar: main0 .* card=[0-9]+,4,4,4 r([1-9][0-9]*) fills=0
expect-log window state margin4-sidebar: main0 .* pageRound=[0-9]+ windowRound=[0-9]+ inside=1
cra://action/toggleSidebar
wait 2
cra://debug?windowState=margin4-hidden
expect-log window state margin4-hidden: main0 .* card=4,4,4,4 r([1-9][0-9]*) fills=0
expect-log window state margin4-hidden: main0 .* inside=1
cra://debug?pageMarginSetting=1
wait 1
cra://debug?windowState=margin1-hidden
expect-log window state margin1-hidden: main0 .* card=1,1,1,1 r([1-9][0-9]*) fills=0 .* inside=1
cra://debug?pageMarginSetting=7
wait 1
cra://debug?windowState=margin7-hidden
expect-log window state margin7-hidden: main0 .* card=7,7,7,7 r([1-9][0-9]*) fills=0
cra://debug?pageMarginSetting=30
wait 1
cra://debug?windowState=margin-clamped
expect-log window state margin-clamped: main0 .* card=10,10,10,10 r6 fills=0 .* inside=1
